          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            was originally conceived as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonlinear+functional"} functional
            on the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+metrics"} pseudo-Riemannian metrics
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connections
            with values in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} Poincaré Lie algebra
            – subject to the constraint that the component in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/translation+Lie+algebra"} translation Lie algebra
            defines a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein+field"} vielbein field
          %p
            Mathematically this means that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            is modeled as a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+connection"} Cartan connection
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+group"} Lorentz group
            inside the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+group"} Poincaré group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            this is known as the
            %em first order formalism
            or the
            = succeed "." do
              %em Cartan moving frame method
            = succeed "-connection" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+Lie+algebra"} Poincaré Lie algebra
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
            and the remainder the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+connection"} spin connection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            of gravity – the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+tensor"} Riemann tensor
            – is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
          %p
            The reformulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+geometry"} pseudo-Riemannian geometry
            in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            is suggestive of also re-rewriting the form of the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            of the theory of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            3+1 one such alternative is known as the
            = succeed "." do
              %em Palatini-Cartan-Holst action
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            coincides with that induced by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Hilbert+action"} Einstein-Hilbert action
            is due to
            %a{:href => "#CattaneoSchiavina17a"} Cattaneo-Schiavina 17a
          %p
            Promoting the first-order formulation of gravity from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+group"} Poincaré group
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+group"} super Poincaré group
            yields
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            formulated in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Cartan+geometry"} super Cartan geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebra+cohomology"} Lie n-algebra
            extensions of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincar%C3%A9+group"} super Poincaré group
            (from the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} brane bouquet
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supergravity"} type II supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+supergravity"} heterotic supergravity
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            in
            = succeed "-formulation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Cartan+geometry"} higher Cartan geometry
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fr%C3%A9+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fré formulation of supergravity
          %div
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry"} geometric
