          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#local_and_global_framing Local and global framing
          %p
            Discussion in the physics literature traditionally tends to ignore the global structure of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            manifolds and pretends that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
            field may be chosen globally, hence that spacetime admits a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framed+manifold"} framing
          %p
            In general that is only valid locally, but it so happens that in the archetypical case of interest, namely for 4-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globally+hyperbolic+spacetimes"} globally hyperbolic spacetimes
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} orientable
            spatial slices, it is valid globally. See
            %em
              %a{:href => "framed+manifold#In4dFirstOrderGravity"} this remark
            at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framed+manifold"} framed manifold
            for more.
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/teleparallel+gravity"} teleparallel gravity
